Package: chutils
Title: Utility Functions for Experimental Psychology Analyses
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R: person(given = "Dale", family = "Cohen", email = "dalejcohen@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Helpers used across the author's analysis packages and scripts:
    data wrangling and subject filtering, model fit statistics, signal
    detection measures, curve fitting for choice and response time data,
    plotting helpers, and assorted small utilities. Functions carry a 'ch.'
    prefix. The scope is deliberately broad; functions with a domain of
    their own belong in a package of their own.
Note: Development of this package was assisted by Claude (Anthropic), an AI
    coding assistant, for code refactoring, documentation, testing, and
    debugging. All scientific decisions, model specifications, and algorithm
    design were made by the package authors.
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
